  "strategy": "1. Approach and Rationale\n   We approach the problem using a bilevel optimization strategy with two distinct phases:\n   - Top-Level: Global shape optimization that places function values strategically to minimize maximum correlation\n   - Bottom-Level: Local refinement optimization that adjusts values within the shape to meet the sum constraint and achieve higher precision\n   This differs from the original sequential refinement by explicitly separating shape optimation from parameter refinement.\n   The core bottleneck addressed is the lack of structured shape optimization in the original approach.\n\n2. Mathematical Specification\n   - Objective: Minimize C\u2085 = max_\u03ba \u222b h(x)(1-h(x+\u03ba)) dx over x,\u03ba \u2208 [0,2]\n   - Constraints: 0 \u2264 h(x) \u2264 1 for all x, \u222b h(x) dx = 1\n   - Shape Optimization: Minimize the maximum correlation by strategically placing function values at coordinates identified by projection optimization\n   - Refinement Optimization: Adjust values to satisfy constraints while maintaining the optimal shape, using logarithmic barriers for feasibility\n\n3. Implementation Procedure\n   - Shape Optimization:\n     Step 1: Initialize grid with 8 points\n     Step 2:\u9879\u76ee\u827d\toptimize shape placement (grid points) using:\n        - objective: function value (optimization direction: min)\n        - constraints: [0,1] shape values\n        - rounding: interpolated parent solution\n        - solver: 'SLSQP' with:\n           bounds=(0.0,1.0) for each grid point\n           constraints: \u2211shape_i/16 = 1\n   - Refinement Optimization:\n     Step 3: For each optimal shape position:\n        - Create local grid interpolation (10 samples)\n        - Project to feasible values\n        - Refine differences using logarithmic barrier optimization\n   - Parameters:\n     - Budget split: 50% shape optimization, 50% refinement\n     - Shape grid: 8 points (8)\n     - Allowed solvers: ['SLSQP', 'Nelder-Mead', 'COBYLA']\n\n4. Search Choices and Variations\n   - Shape Optimization:\n     InitialShapeGrid = 8\n     ObjectiveFunction: -np.logspace(-np.abs(param),-np.abs(param)/3,5) fal1\n     alpha_sequence = [4,2,0.5,0.1] # Main improvement sequence\n     max_iterations = 100\n   - Refinement Optimization:\n     Initial points: 12\n     Objective type: -Uniform\n     Local iterations: 50\n   - Variations:\n     - Phase 1: Binary search (enable/disable based on improvement rate)\n     - Phase 2: Central force optimization (projection-based)\n     - Phase 3: Gaussian process surrogate (for late stages)\n\n5. Compute Budget and Robustness\n   - Phase 1 (shape optimization):\n     Wall time budget: 50% of total time\n     Parameters: Trial division optimization, max 500 function evaluations\n   - Feasibility maintenance:\n     Damage control: Restart if stuck (using initialization)\n     Budget check: Early termination if remaining time < 10 seconds/point\n     \u843d\u8dd1     Failure recovery: Return interpolated solution if stuck\n   - Performance control:\n     Early exit if improvement < 1e-11 after 50 iterations\n     Per-period statistical evaluation (return best candidate)\n\n6. Validation and Return Contract\n   - Feasibility validation:\n     - 0 \u2264 values[i] \u2264 1 for all i with tolerance 1e-5\n     - Finite target value with tolerance 1e-10\n   - Output sanitation:\n     - h_values: Projected to feasible via final adjustment\n     - C5: max correlation * dx (computed separately)\n     - Harmony: Consistent implementation with provided functions\n   - Termination conditions:\n     - Time expiration with best candidate retention\n     - Local lock indication (useful neighborhood search)\n     - Direct comparison of correlation values",
